'''''Veronica epacridea''''', [[Synonym (taxonomy)|synonym]] '''''Hebe epacridea''''', is a plant of the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Plantaginaceae]].<ref name="POWO_811955-1">{{cite web |title=''Veronica epacridea'' Hook.f.. |work=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:811955-1 |access-date=2022-10-09 }}</ref> It is [[endemic (ecology)|endemic]] to altitudes above 3,000 feet from the [[Marlborough Region]] to [[Otago]] region on the [[South Island]] of New Zealand. It is a low-growing, evergreen shrub, reaching 10&nbsp;cm in height, with thick, closely placed, recurved green leaves that are 5–7&nbsp;mm long. Flowers are white.

